.TH MU2EDAQ\-DISCOVER\-GUI 1 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-discovery 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-discover\-gui \- graphical browser for discoverable Mu2e DAQ resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-discover\-gui
.RB [ \-\-filter
.IR KEY=GLOB ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-retries
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-group
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR ip ]
.RB [ \-\-broadcast
.IR addr ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-broadcast ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-auto ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-discover\-gui
sends the same DISCOVER query as
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
(protocol
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery/1 ,
group 239.255.42.99, UDP port 28999), by multicast and by subnet broadcast
together, and displays every ANNOUNCE reply in a table.
The status bar names the transports each probe used, so a scan that shows only
the local switch's nodes is recognisable as multicast confined by IGMP
snooping.
.PP
The table shows all published parameters of each resource. The core
fields
.RB ( name ", " app ", " host ", " port ", " scheme ", " version ", "
.BR pid ", " started ", " id )
come first; any additional parameters a responder publishes in its
.B meta
map appear as further
.BI meta. key
columns, discovered at run time.
.PP
Rows are grouped by resource class: every instance that shares an
.B app
value is collected under a bold class row showing the instance count.
Classes can be expanded and collapsed individually or with the
.B Expand All
and
.B Collapse All
toolbar buttons.
.PP
Clicking a column header sorts by that field; clicking again reverses
the order.
.B port
and
.B pid
sort numerically, everything else sorts case\-insensitively as text.
Sorting applies to the class rows and to the instances within each
class. Column order can be rearranged by dragging headers.
.PP
Resources that advertise the same
.IR host : port
pair are treated as a conflict and drawn in bold red, with a tooltip
naming the contested endpoint. The status bar reports how many
conflicts were flagged.
.PP
If no resource replies, the table shows a single
.B "No resources found"
row and the status bar names the group and port that were probed.
.SH CONTEXT MENU
Right\-clicking a resource row offers:
.TP
.B Copy Record (Plain Text)
The whole record as aligned
.RI "" field " : " value
lines.
.TP
.B Copy Record (JSON)
The whole record as indented JSON, exactly as it came off the wire.
.TP
.BI "Copy \(dq" field "\(dq"
The value of the single field under the cursor.
.TP
.B Copy Field
A submenu with every published field of that record; choosing one
copies just that value.
.PP
Right\-clicking a class row instead offers
.B Copy Class (Plain Text)
and
.BR "Copy Class (JSON)" ,
covering every instance of that class.
.B Copy All Resources
(text or JSON) and
.B Probe Again
are always available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " KEY=GLOB"
Pre\-fill the toolbar filter. Keys:
.BR app ", " name ", " host .
Values are fnmatch\-style globs (e.g.\&
.BR app=vnc ).
The filter can be changed in the window at any time; press Enter to
re\-probe.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
How long each probe waits for replies. Default 2.0.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " n"
Number of query transmissions per probe. Default 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-group " addr"
Multicast group. Default 239.255.42.99.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
UDP port. Default 28999.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " ip"
Local interface address to send the multicast and broadcast from. Useful on
multi\-homed DAQ nodes.
.TP
.BI \-\-broadcast " addr"
Also broadcast each probe to
.IR addr ;
repeatable. Default 255.255.255.255, the local subnet. This is what lets the
browser see nodes on other switches, where IGMP snooping without a querier
stops the multicast; see
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-broadcast
Multicast only, as before version 1.1.0.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " seconds"
Auto\-probe interval. Default 10.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Start with auto\-probing enabled (equivalent to ticking
.B Auto
in the toolbar).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
YAML configuration file; see
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1).
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B F5
Probe now.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/discovery.yaml
The packaged example configuration.
Read only when named by
.B \-\-config
or
.BR MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG ;
there is no fixed default path.
The
.B interval
key is used only by this command.
.TP
.I src/mu2edaq_discovery/assets/mu2edaq-discovery.png
The packaged window and application icon.
.TP
.I ./start-mu2edaq-discover-gui.sh
Creates or updates
.I venv/
with the
.B gui
extra and launches the GUI; arguments are passed straight through.
.TP
.I ./stop-mu2edaq-discover-gui.sh
Sends SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after five seconds, to any running instance.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command line options override these; they in turn override the config file,
which overrides the built\-in defaults.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_GROUP
Multicast group.
Default 239.255.42.99.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_PORT
UDP port.
Default 28999.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT
Seconds each probe waits for replies.
Default 2.0.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_BROADCAST
Broadcast destinations, spelled as for
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_INTERVAL
Auto\-probe interval in seconds.
Default 10.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG
Default value of
.BR \-\-config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal window close.
.TP
.B 1
No Qt binding installed, an unsupported
.B \-\-filter
key, a config file that needs PyYAML when PyYAML is absent, or an invalid
broadcast setting.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line, from the argument parser.
.SH EXAMPLES
Browse everything, re\-probing every 15 seconds:
.EX
    mu2edaq\-discover\-gui \-\-auto \-\-interval 15
.EE
Start filtered to the VNC sessions:
.EX
    mu2edaq\-discover\-gui \-\-filter app=vnc
.EE
On a multi\-homed node, probe both DAQ subnets:
.EX
    mu2edaq\-discover\-gui \-\-broadcast 131.225.245.255 \-\-broadcast 10.226.9.255
.EE
.SH NOTES
A Qt binding is required:
.B PyQt6
(preferred) or
.BR PySide6 ;
install with
.BR "pip install 'mu2edaq-discovery[gui]'" .
.PP
Neither multicast nor broadcast traverses the FNAL gateway.
Run the GUI on a cluster node, over X11 forwarding or in a VNC session, to see
on\-site resources.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1),
.BR mu2edaq_discovery (3),
.BR discovery.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery (7)
